{
  "name": "Privacy Request (DSAR): GDPR and CCPA",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Privacy request (DSAR) automation: GDPR and CCPA\nHandles **access**, **erasure** and **correction** requests for workplace data in Slack, Google Workspace and Jira, under **GDPR** (EU/EEA) or **CCPA/CPRA** (California), from intake to closure.\n\n### How it works\n1. A webhook receives the request. The jurisdiction's rules set the deadline: one month under GDPR, 45 days under CCPA, both from receipt.\n2. The request is logged to a Google Sheets register.\n3. The requester is emailed an acknowledgment with the deadline and a verification link (7 days to click). Under CCPA this meets the 10-business-day acknowledgment rule.\n4. The person is looked up in Slack, Google Workspace and Jira.\n5. **Access:** a JSON export is emailed. **Erasure:** a DPO approves in Slack before anything is deleted. **Correction:** the privacy team makes the change and confirms. Refusals explain the reason and where to complain.\n6. The register is updated with the outcome.\n\nPair with **DSAR Deadline Monitor** for daily overdue alerts.\n\n### Setup\n1. Fill in **Workflow Configuration** (sheet ID, sender address, Jira URL).\n2. Add credentials: SMTP, Slack API (`users:read.email`, `chat:write`), Google OAuth2 with Admin SDK Directory access, Jira Software Cloud, and Header Auth for the Slack SCIM and Atlassian admin APIs.\n3. Create a Google Sheet with a `DSARRegister` tab and the columns RequestId, Jurisdiction, RequestType, Email, ReceivedAt, AcknowledgedAt, Deadline, Status, SystemsFound, CompletedAt.\n4. Create the Slack channel `#privacy-approvals`.\n\n### Add a jurisdiction\nAdd an entry to `RULES` in **Normalize Request**: deadline, extension, acknowledgment window, legal references and complaint wording.\n\n### Limitations\n- A technical template, not legal advice. Review rules and wording with your DPO or counsel.\n- Business days skip weekends but not public holidays.\n- Slack SCIM needs a Business+ or Enterprise Grid plan. Deleting a Google user is permanent: transfer Drive files first.\n\nExample request body:\n`{\"jurisdiction\": \"CCPA\", \"requestType\": \"access\", \"email\": \"jane@example.com\"}`",
        "height": 1180,
        "width": 580
      },
      "id": "109fbb05-61f9-581c-af4c-dfde5a0935a7",
